WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:10.460
In 1934, a scientist named Gause published his counts of two kinds of paramecium

2
00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:12.040
grown in one tube.

3
00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:17.740
Paramecia are tiny one-celled living things that swim in water.

4
00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:19.760
They ate bacteria.

5
00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:22.520
Each kind grew well alone.

6
00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:28.500
Together, one kind stayed common, and the other shrank to a small number.

7
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:30.400
Here is the question.

8
00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:35.820
Why do some living things fight over food, while others share it?

9
00:00:36.533 --> 00:00:40.013
Every living thing needs matter and energy.

10
00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:42.473
Animals get both from food.

11
00:00:43.953 --> 00:00:48.073
Competition happens when living things need the same resource, and there is not

12
00:00:48.073 --> 00:00:55.153
enough for all. Animals compete for food, water, shelter, territory and mates.

13
00:00:56.613 --> 00:00:59.393
Territory is the area an animal keeps others out of.

14
00:01:00.133 --> 00:01:02.293
Competition is often quiet.

15
00:01:02.933 --> 00:01:03.933
Nobody has to fight.

16
00:01:04.653 --> 00:01:06.893
The paramecia ate the same bacteria.

17
00:01:07.793 --> 00:01:10.773
Bacteria eaten by one kind were gone for the other.

18
00:01:11.893 --> 00:01:16.453
A population is all the members of one species living in one area.

19
00:01:17.433 --> 00:01:21.953
Members of a population often compete, like robins hunting worms on one lawn.

20
00:01:23.113 --> 00:01:26.213
Plants compete too, for light, water and minerals.

21
00:01:27.267 --> 00:01:30.327
Living things can also cooperate.

22
00:01:31.207 --> 00:01:35.967
Cooperation is when members of a population work together to meet their needs.

23
00:01:37.087 --> 00:01:40.447
A honeybee colony can hold tens of thousands of bees.

24
00:01:41.447 --> 00:01:45.887
Workers do different jobs, like caring for young and guarding the hive.

25
00:01:46.727 --> 00:01:49.147
They pass liquid food from bee to bee.

26
00:01:49.927 --> 00:01:51.747
The shares are not always equal.

27
00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:58.520
A limiting factor is anything in the environment that limits how many of a species

28
00:01:58.520 --> 00:01:59.780
can live in a place.

29
00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:05.060
A biotic factor is a living part, like food or disease.

30
00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:10.840
An abiotic factor is a nonliving part, like water or temperature.

31
00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:16.200
A community is all the populations in an area that interact.

32
00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:22.640
If a disease killed many rabbits, foxes that eat rabbits would find less food.

33
00:02:23.533 --> 00:02:28.973
So why do some living things fight over food, while others share it?

34
00:02:29.793 --> 00:02:33.973
Some compete for the same limited resource, often without any fight.

35
00:02:34.993 --> 00:02:40.933
Others cooperate. And limiting factors, living and nonliving, set how many can

36
00:02:40.933 --> 00:02:41.533
live in a place.
